# MVI Contract Pattern

Every screen has a Contract object with exactly three nested types:

```kotlin
object {Feature}Contract {
    data class State(
        val isLoading: Boolean = false,
        val error: String? = null,
        // feature-specific fields with sensible defaults
    ) : UiState

    sealed interface Intent : UiIntent {
        data object Load{Feature} : Intent          // initial load
        data object Refresh : Intent                 // pull-to-refresh
        data class Select{Item}(val id: String) : Intent  // navigation
        // use data object for no-arg, data class for parameterized
    }

    sealed interface Effect : UiEffect {
        data class NavigateTo{Screen}(val id: String) : Effect
        data class ShowSnackbar(val message: String) : Effect
    }
}
```

## Rules
- State implements `UiState`, Intent implements `UiIntent`, Effect implements `UiEffect`
- All State fields must have default values (supports `State()` construction)
- Navigation triggers → Effect (one-shot), UI state changes → State
- Computed properties in State via `get()` (e.g., `val hasData: Boolean get() = data != null`)
- One file per screen: `{Feature}Contract.kt` in `presentation/{feature}/`
